2026:09:01,Katowice,1,Katowice Wojciech Korfanty Airport,Międzynarodowy Port Lotniczy Katowice,"50.471226495210026, 19.07402076361477","Katowice Wojciech Korfanty Arpt, Wolności 90/Terminal A, 42-625 Pyrzowice, Poland","Katowice Airport (tram, bus)",Transport system,5,,"Katowice Wojciech Korfanty Airport is an international airport, located in Pyrzowice, 30 km (19 mi) north of Katowice, Poland. The airport is named after Wojciech Korfanty, a politician of the early years of Polish independence. It is the fourth-busiest airport in Poland by passenger volumes, with just shy of 7.3 million passengers in 2025. It is also the second-busiest airport in the country by cargo volume and the largest origin of charter flights in Poland."
2026:09:01,Katowice,2,Katowice,Katowice,"50.25817742310977, 19.017500228181564","50.25817742310977, 19.017500228181564","Katowice Dworzec (tram, bus)",Transport system,5,,"Katowice railway station is a railway station in Katowice, Silesia, Poland, and the largest railway station in the Upper Silesian Industrial Region. Domestic and international trains connect at the station to most major cities in Europe; these are operated primarily by Polskie Koleje Państwowe."
2026:09:01,Katowice,3,Międzynarodowy Dworzec Autobusowy,Międzynarodowy Dworzec Autobusowy,"50.258941903512216, 19.01060332411177","Sądowa 5, 40-078 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Sobieskiego (tram),Transport system,5,,"The Filharmonia Śląska w Katowicach is a music institution in Katowice, Silesia, Poland. The Silesian Philharmonic in Katowice was founded in 1945. The first concert of the orchestra took place on 26 of May 1945. A mixed choir was added in 1973."
2026:09:01,Katowice,4,Nikiszowiec,Nikiszowiec,"50.24771110180893, 19.071216066119447",,Katowice Zawodzie (train),Historical Sites,5,,Nikiszowiec is a well-known neighbourhood and settlement which is part of the Janów-Nikiszowiec administrative district of the city of Katowice.
2026:09:01,Katowice,5,Silesian Museum,Muzeum Śląskie,"50.263536513070434, 19.034275587019025","Tadeusza Dobrowolskiego 1, 40-205 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Strefa Kultury Muzeum Śląskie (bus),Museums,5,,"The Polish National Radio Symphony Orchestra is one of Poland's radio orchestras and premier musical institutions. It was founded in 1935 in Warsaw and was later re-established in Katowice in 1945. Since 2006 it has been a ""National Cultural Institution""."
2026:09:01,Katowice,6,Spodek,Spodek,"50.266053071551944, 19.025369896850584","al. Wojciecha Korfantego 35, 40-161 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Rondo (tram),Culture,10,,"Spodek is a multipurpose arena complex in Katowice, Poland, opened on 9 May 1971. Aside from the main dome, the complex includes a gym, an ice rink, a hotel and three large car parks. It was the largest indoor venue of its kind in Poland until it was surpassed by Tauron Arena in 2014."
2026:09:01,Katowice,7,National Polish Radio Symphony Orchestra,Narodowa Orkiestra Symfoniczna Polskiego Radia w Katowicach,"50.26406607155716, 19.028022267980635","plac Wojciecha Kilara 1, 40-202 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Strefa Kultury NOSPR (bus),Culture,10,,"The Headquarters of the Polish National Radio Symphony Orchestra in Katowice is a concert hall located at 1 Wojciech Kilar Square in the Bogucice district of Katowice, Poland. It serves as the home of the Polish National Radio Symphony Orchestra.It is also a main component of the Katowice Culture Zone, which also includes the International Congress Centre and the Silesian Museum."
2026:09:01,Katowice,8,Bajka Pana Kleksa,Bajka Pana Kleksa,"50.255146111860796, 19.06160052565104","Porcelanowa 23, 40-246 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Fabryka Porcelany (bus),Family & Kids Entertainment,10,,"Zawodzie is a part and a district of Katowice, located in the central-eastern section of the city, between Bogucice, Dąbrówka Mała, Janów-Nikiszowiec, Osiedle Paderewskiego-Muchowiec, and Śródmieście, along the Rawa river. The district is multifunctional, with a well-developed industrial sector, including a rich tradition of metallurgy. Due to the presence of the University of Economics in the district, it also has a well-developed higher education sector."
2026:09:01,Katowice,9,Valley of the Three Ponds,Dolina Trzech Stawów,"50.24924139264709, 19.04758629681519","Trzech Stawów, 40-289 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Porcelanowa (bus),Parks & Nature,10,,"The Valley of Three Ponds is a large park and wooded area in the southern part of the city of Katowice, Poland. The name comes from the existence of three large ponds in the park area."
2026:09:01,Katowice,10,Immaculate Conception of the Blessed Virgin Mary,Kościół Rzymskokatolicki Niepokalanego Poczęcia Najświętszej Marii Panny,"50.25714555274322, 19.030275196815694","plac Szramka 1, 40-014 Katowice, Poland","Katowice Szkoła Filmowa UŚ 9tram, bus)",Historical Sites,10,,"St. Mary's Church in Katowice is one of the oldest churches in Katowice, Poland, dating back to 19th century. This neo-Gothic church is located in the Śródmieście district. The architectural design was entrusted to Alexis Langer, a renowned architect from Breslau (Wrocław). Although the original plans envisioned a much grander scale, the final neo-Gothic building spans 43 meters in length and 31 meters in width. Its most distinctive feature is the 71-meter octagonal tower, a signature trademark of Langer's craftsmanship."
2026:09:01,Katowice,11,Guitar History Museum,Muzeum Historii Gitary,"50.25553297155564, 19.01672899681556","Krzywa 4, 40-061 Katowice, Poland","Katowice Plac Miarki (tram, bus)",Museums,15,,Katowice Voivodeship can refer to one of two political entities in Poland:
2026:09:01,Katowice,12,Museum of the History of Katowice,Muzeum Historii Katowic,"50.25534383122282, 19.028462996815627","Szafranka 9, 40-025 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Akademia Muzyczna (bus),Museums,15,,"The Karol Szymanowski Academy of Music is a school of music of university level in Katowice, in Poland. It is named for Karol Szymanowski."
2026:09:01,Katowice,13,Mariacka,Mariacka,"50.25731318640494, 19.028084514548222","40-014 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Mariacka (bus),Shopping & Services,15,,"Warszawska Street in Katowice is a street in the centre of Katowice. The street was built in the 19th century. Until 1922 and during World War II the street was called Friedrichstraße, 1926–1939 Marszałka Piłsudskiego."
2026:09:01,Katowice,14,Pixel XL,Pixel XL,"50.26279157155697, 19.020291967980594","Sokolska 31, 40-086 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Piotra Skargi (bus),Family & Kids Entertainment,15,,"Katowice is the capital city of the Silesian Voivodeship in southern Poland and the central city of the Katowice urban area. As of 2021, Katowice has an official population of 286,960, and a resident population estimate of around 315,000. The Katowice metropolitan area has a population of 2.5 million, and is part of a larger Katowice–Ostrava metropolitan area that extends into the Czech Republic and has a population of around 5 million people."
2026:09:01,Katowice,15,Silesian Insurgents' Monument,Pomnik Powstańców Śląskich,"50.26359798851551, 19.024016067980654","al. Wojciecha Korfantego, 40-959 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Rondo (tram),Historical Sites,15,,"The Silesian Insurgents Memorial in Katowice, southern Poland, it is a monument to those who took part in the three Silesian Uprisings of 1919, 1920 and 1921. These uprisings aimed to make the region of Upper Silesia part of the newly independent Polish state. It is located nearby to the Spodek."
2026:09:01,Katowice,16,Kosciuszko Park,Park Kościuszki,"50.245918293603204, 19.004643796814975","Tadeusza Kościuszki, 40-001 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Kościuszki Basen (tram),Parks & Nature,20,,"The Kościuszko Park, which has existed since 1925, is one of the most famous and frequented parks in Katowice, Poland. It is situated at the street of the same name."
2026:09:01,Katowice,17,Market Square,Katowice Rynek,"50.26006028576474, 19.022362744412916","40-003 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Rynek /Teatr Śl./ (tram),Old Town,20,,"Silesian Museum in Katowice is a museum in the city of Katowice, Poland."
2026:09:01,Katowice,18,Wilson Shaft Gallery,Szyb Wilson w Katowicach,"50.250650131897814, 19.083519096815255","Oswobodzenia 1, 40-403 Katowice, Poland",Nikiszowiec Szyb Wilson (bus),Museums,20,,"Szyb Wilson Gallery is a contemporary art gallery in Katowice, Poland, located at 1 Oswobodzenia Street in the Janów-Nikiszowiec district. It was opened in 2001 in the revitalized building of the pithead and bathhouse of the Wilson shafts of the Wieczorek Coal Mine, whose history dates back to 1826."
2026:09:01,Katowice,19,"Archcathedral of Christ the King, Katowice",Archikatedra Chrystusa Króla,"50.251483551111875, 19.019594058182843","Plebiscytowa 49A, 40-041 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Jordana (tram),Historical Sites,20,,"Archikatedra Chrystusa Króla w Katowicach is a classicist and modernist archcathedral in Katowice-Śródmieście, Katowice, Poland. Constructed between 1927 and 1955, the Archcathedral of Christ the King is the largest archcathedral and cathedral in Poland, 120,000 metres cubed large."
2026:09:01,Katowice,20,House of Fear Asylum,Dom Strachu Asylum,"50.25989727155963, 19.016464296704562","3 Maja 23, 40-096 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Plac Wolności (tram),Museums,20,,"3 Maja Street in Katowice is a street in the centre ('Śródmieście') of Katowice, Poland. The street was built in the 19th century. During World War II the street was called Grundmannstraße, 1867−1922 Grundmannstraße, 1856−1867 Industriestraße."
2026:09:01,Katowice,21,Giszowiec Osiedle,Giszowiec Osiedle,"50.22200154659118, 19.06826976432765","Katowice, Poland",Giszowiec Osiedle (bus),Parks & Nature,25,,
2026:09:01,Katowice,22,Silesia City Center,Silesia City Center,"50.27052188749162, 19.00525387321638","Chorzowska 107, 40-101 Katowice, Poland",Dąb Silesia City Center (tram),Shopping & Services,25,,"Silesia City Center is a shopping mall in Katowice, Silesia, Poland. It was opened in 2005 as the first modern shopping mall in Katowice. In 2015 it has been described as the ""largest shopping mall in the Silesia region""."
2026:09:01,Katowice,23,Muzeum Hutnictwa Cynku WALCOWNIA,Muzeum Hutnictwa Cynku WALCOWNIA,"50.26371141309583, 19.081141039145177","11 Listopada 50, 40-387 Katowice, Poland",Szopienice Muzeum Walcownia (bus),Museums,25,,"Szopienice-Burowiec is a district of Katowice, Poland, located in the north-eastern part of the city. It has an area of 8.47 km2 and in 2007 had 17,139 inhabitants."
2026:09:01,Katowice,24,Silesian Freedom and Solidarity Centre,Śląskie Centrum Wolności i Solidarności,"50.24420659409573, 18.99003986797944","Wincentego Pola 38, 40-596 Katowice, Poland",Brynów Kopalnia Wujek (bus),Museums,25,,"Wujek Coal Mine is a coal mine in Katowice, Poland. It is widely known in Poland as the place of the massacre of striking miners in 1981, as well as being the site of a deadly mining accident in 2009."
2026:09:01,Katowice,25,Museum of the History of Computers and Information Technology,Muzeum Historii Komputerów i Informatyki Siedziba główna,"50.252890521608045, 19.022579996815413","Henryka Sienkiewicza 28, 40-061 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Powstańców Przychodnie (bus),Museums,25,,Polish Radio Katowice is the largest regional station of Polish Radio. It was created in 1927. It can be received in the Silesian Voivodeship and bordering entities.
2026:09:01,Katowice,26,Katowice Cultural Zone,Katowicka Strefa Kultury,"50.26527455508568, 19.029989196816235","Henryka Mikołaja Góreckiego, Katowice, Poland",Katowice Rondo (tram),Culture,30,,"The Headquarters of the Polish National Radio Symphony Orchestra in Katowice is a concert hall located at 1 Wojciech Kilar Square in the Bogucice district of Katowice, Poland. It serves as the home of the Polish National Radio Symphony Orchestra.It is also a main component of the Katowice Culture Zone, which also includes the International Congress Centre and the Silesian Museum."
2026:09:01,Katowice,27,Laserhouse,Laserhouse,"50.257165055748544, 19.01191190846102","Kamienna 9, 40-067 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Mikołowska Sąd )bus),Museums,30,,"The Pałac Goldsteinów or Goldstein Palace is neo-Renaissance palace, which was built by two brothers, Abraham and Joseph Goldstein. It is located in Katowice, Silesia, Poland, at the west end of the city centre, at 50°15′33″N 19°0′47″E."
2026:09:01,Katowice,28,Church of Sts. Michael the Archangel,Kościół Rzymskokatolicki pw. św. Michała Archanioła,"50.240959409859464, 19.004803039002887","Tadeusza Kościuszki, Katowice, Poland",Katowice Kościuszki Basen (tram),Historical Sites,30,,"Church of St. Michael Archangel is one of the oldest buildings in Katowice. It is located in Kościuszko Park, where it was moved in 1938 from the village Syrynia, where it was originally constructed in 1510. It is under the invocation of St. Michael."
2026:09:01,Katowice,29,Orange Club Katowice,Klub Pomarańcza,"50.25987603057098, 19.02100663914492","Adama Mickiewicza 4, 40-092 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Rynek (tram),Bars & Clubs,30,,"Market Square in Katowice is a central feature of the Śródmieście district in the city of Katowice, Poland. This market square, the main one in the city, dates to the late 19th century. It has been rebuilt several times, with the latest round of changes currently in progress. During the communist era, some of the historic buildings were demolished to make way for modern service facilities. A characteristic feature of the square is a network of streetcar tracks, crossing the square in several directions. There are three squares within the marketplace: Kwiatowy, Teatralny, and Obrońców Katowic."
2026:09:01,Katowice,30,Gallery of Fine Arts in Katowice RONDO ART,Rondo Sztuki - Galeria ASP,"50.26450951321076, 19.02343305018951","Rondo im. gen. Jerzego Ziętka 1, 40-001 Katowice, Poland",Katowice Rondo (tram),Culture,30,,"The Rondo Generała Jerzego Ziętka in Katowice is the roundabout in the centre of the city, in the Silesian Voivodship in southern Poland. On that main traffic circle, the Aleja Korfantego and the road 79, part of the Drogowa Trasa Średnicowa, meet."
2026:09:01,Katowice,31,BioBazar Huta Baildon,BioBazar Huta Baildon,"50.26792882941302, 18.994232867980923","Johna Baildona 66, 40-115 Katowice, Poland",Załęże Dwór (bus),Markets,40,,"Załęże is a part and a district of Katowice, located in the north-western part of the city, in the central part of the Upper Silesian conurbation, on the Rawa river. It runs along Gliwicka Street in a characteristic, winding course from the city center to the border of Chorzów. It also borders Osiedle Tysiąclecia, Dąb, Śródmieście, Załęska Hałda-Brynów, and Osiedle Witosa."
